This commit pins the FORMAT.md the file follows (cpe/tools/dao-lift/FORMAT.md at that commit);
areas/access/sync/store/src/vocab.rs records the same commit.

Regenerate from the incubator's cpe/ directory, at the commit above, on the unzipped dump:

  cargo run --locked --release --manifest-path tools/dao-lift/Cargo.toml -- snapshot <dump-dir> <out.nq>

The output is byte-identical for the same dump. Moving the pin means moving it here and in vocab.rs
together, regenerating, and keeping sync-store's committed-file tests green without changing their
expectations: those come from the dump. Every row of 0803-curation.csv names a resource of this file.
If a regenerated file drops one, sync-store refuses the whole project until the row is removed or
re-keyed by hand.

0803-arks.txt: the 0803 data ARKs Incunabula stores, which are dao-lift's output. One plain data ARK
per line, sorted, 4,143 lines.

Source
  file:            cpe/projects/incunabula/data.sql (the resources.ark and annotations.ark columns)
  repository:      dasch-swiss/dsp-incubator, at commit c2b3e10a8d7c695347e11ed7a5cf31bf0f3dca64

Extract it in the incubator checkout at that commit:

  grep -oE 'https://ark\.dasch\.swiss/ark:/72163/1/0803/[A-Za-z0-9_=]+' cpe/projects/incunabula/data.sql | LC_ALL=C sort -u

It is a subset of the served resources: no LinkObj, 64 of 77 Regions, no calibration-scan Pages. The
committed tests check each line against the served ARK. Like 0803.nq, it is a frozen copy and does not
follow the incubator.

0803-curation.csv: the curation of project 0803 that sync-store serves beside 0803.nq: what the
project's editors authored about single resources. One row per resource, 138 lines with the header.
Hand-authored: it is edited in place by a person and never regenerated.

Source
  files:           cpe/projects/incunabula/raw/curation.csv
                   cpe/projects/incunabula/raw/annotation-curation.csv
                   cpe/projects/incunabula/raw/pages.csv
                   cpe/projects/incunabula/translate.py:1030-1031 (UNSIGNED_STRIP_ID, UNSIGNED_STRIP_NAME)
  repository:      dasch-swiss/dsp-incubator, at commit 6e8e4063b54603f4615a6ed96025362a37dae70b

Mapping
  curation.csv, one row per Book, in file order
    dsp_id                             iri, as http://rdfh.ch/0803/<dsp_id>
    id                                 slug
    date_display                       date_display@de
    office, title_override, sort_key   the same key
    cover_page (a pages.csv id)        cover_page, as that Page's IRI
    teaser_de, teaser_en               teaser@de, teaser@en
  annotation-curation.csv, one row per Region or LinkObj, in file order
    id                                 iri, as http://rdfh.ch/0803/<id>
    keep, lang, name                   the same key
    note                               #note, a comment column, never served
    kind                               dropped: it restates the resource's class
  translate.py, the last row, the Band http://rdfh.ch/0803/EJZQcYisXECHxchG_KQ27w
    UNSIGNED_STRIP_ID                  slug
    UNSIGNED_STRIP_NAME                name

pages.csv has no IRI column. A Page's IRI is http://rdfh.ch/0803/ followed by the last path segment of
its ark cell, without the check digit (the last character) and with every = turned into -. Every value
is copied verbatim.

The file was derived once, by a script that is not kept, and is edited by hand from then on: it is not
regenerated. Until DEV-7402 lands, the incubator's CSV files stay authoritative for the public
prototype, and nothing checks the two copies against each other. A curation change is made there and
repeated here by hand.
